WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
INTRO:
Most of us think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:07.140
of Saudi Arabia as the oil kingdom. They’re one&nbsp;
of the most dominant voices in the industry and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:12.600
they profit hundreds of billions of dollars every&nbsp;
single year from pumping out oil. But, something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.200
that many of us overlook is that Saudi Arabia is&nbsp;
also the Islamic kingdom. Saudi Arabia is home to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.960
Mecca which is said to be the holiest of Islamic&nbsp;
cities. The founder of Islam, Muhammed the Prophet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:31.320
was not only born in Mecca but this is also where&nbsp;
he had his revelations way back in the early 7th&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.640
century. Given this religious signficance,&nbsp;
I don’t think you’d be surprised to hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.520
that most Muslims try to pilgrimge to this holy&nbsp;
city atleast once their lifetimes. This is what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:47.340
leads to an influx of millions of pilgrims to the&nbsp;
country an on annual basis. For the longest time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:54.060
the only way you could even get into Saudi Arabia&nbsp;
was to either be a pilgrim or have a work Visa. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:59.520
wasn’t till September of 2019 that Saudi Arabia&nbsp;
started accepting tourists. But, even today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:05.520
Mecca is restricted to only Muslims and trying&nbsp;
to sneak in like Airrack is taken extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.740
seriously. Hearing all this, you would think&nbsp;
that Saudi Arabia would also be super keen on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:17.160
protecting the city’s cultural and architectural&nbsp;
history. But, this is actually not the case. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:22.860
fact, Saudi Arabia has been actively destroying&nbsp;
Mecca’s architecture for decades. Since 1985,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:28.920
Saudi Arabia has destroyed 98% of their historical&nbsp;
and religious sites, the vast majority of which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:36.420
was in Mecca. If this number were 5 or 10%, you&nbsp;
may be able to argue that there’s no agenda. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:43.020
at 98%, there’s clearly something going on&nbsp;
here. One researcher puts it as “It’s as if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:48.600
they wanted to wipe out history.” And it’s not&nbsp;
like they’re building new religious sites on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:53.340
top of these ruins either. More times than&nbsp;
not, they’re building hotels and resorts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:58.860
and sometimes it’s a lot worse. For example, they&nbsp;
destroyed the house of the Prophet’s first wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:05.700
in order to build public toilets. I mean, at&nbsp;
this point, they’re just being insulting. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.540
why in the world is Saudi Arabia&nbsp;
destroying their cultural heritage?

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.640
WAHHABISM:&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:20.520
Taking a look back, the destruction of Mecca&nbsp;
is not a new phenomenon by any means. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:27.060
it has been an ongoing trend for nearly a thousand&nbsp;
years dating as far back as 1205. While it’s been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.520
a long time since then, the reasoning behind&nbsp;
current destruction is not that different. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.034
all comes to down to the beliefs of one sector&nbsp;
of Islam called Wahhabism which is a part of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.034 --> 00:02:40.020
the broader Sunni sector. Wahhabism is the&nbsp;
prevailing form of Islam across Saudi Arabia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:45.480
and they’re not fans of worshipping people.&nbsp;
Visiting the shrines and tombs of even prophets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:50.940
and saints is heavily frowned upon. It’s thought&nbsp;
that visiting such places will result in Islam’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:57.360
gravest sin which is to worship anyone other&nbsp;
than god. This does make sense to a degree. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.220
millions of people visit the homes and tombs of&nbsp;
religious figures, it’s only natural that some of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.980
them start to see these religious figures as god&nbsp;
themselves. But, while that is a risk, it does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:12.420
seem rather harsh to wipe out centuries worth of&nbsp;
heritage just to prevent a few from quote on quote&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:17.700
“going out of line”. The way that Saudi Arabia&nbsp;
justifies this is by building structures that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.980
support their view of Islam. Just because Saudi&nbsp;
Arabia has been destroying most of Mecca does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:28.260
mean that they’re looking to destroy all of Mecca.&nbsp;
When it comes to sites that they believe are truly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:33.720
pure and holy like the Kaaba, they not only&nbsp;
protect it, but they try their best to enhance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:39.060
it. Over the years, Saudi Arabia has poured tens&nbsp;
of billions of dollars into the Kaaba and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.560
buildings that surround it. A perfect example&nbsp;
of this is the glorious clock tower that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.180
built right next to the grand Mosque of Mecca.&nbsp;
Not only does the clock tower look magnificent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:54.060
but it has extraordinary capacity. The main tower&nbsp;
itself has over 16 million square feet of floor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.060 --> 00:04:00.720
area and contains 1,618 rooms. Hearing this, I&nbsp;
don’t think you’d be surprised to hear that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:07.620
cost $15 billion to construct. And this is just&nbsp;
one of their many Hajj related projects. They’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:12.600
build several top of the line hotels, parking&nbsp;
garages, restaurants, and everything else that you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:17.400
might need to have a positive pilgrimage. They’ve&nbsp;
also spent substantial time and resources trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:23.520
to expand the area that surrounds the Kaaba. This&nbsp;
way, more people can visit on an annual basis. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.080
most recent expansion project was completed in&nbsp;
2018 which brought the total size of the Great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:34.920
Mosque to a 187 acres, capable of supporting&nbsp;
2.5 million worshippers. As you can see, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:41.640
Saudi Royal family is by no means anti-Islam. If&nbsp;
anything, they’re actually massive supporters, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:47.340
the key thing to note is that they only support&nbsp;
their view of Islam. Historically, they had no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:52.200
issues just blatantly raiding and destroying&nbsp;
people of different sects. But, in modern times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:57.180
Saudi Arabia’s approach to the situation has&nbsp;
become more sophisticated. They’re not destroying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.180 --> 00:05:01.980
these cultural sites just to destroy them. They’re&nbsp;
destroying them so that they can build structures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:07.320
that support Wahhabi Islam. By framing it like&nbsp;
this, the Saudis have been able to shift focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.600
away from their destruction of heritage and move&nbsp;
it over to their construction of heritage. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:17.160
this framing has allowed them continue their&nbsp;
destruction with substantially less backlash.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:21.180
THIRST FOR POWER:&nbsp;

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:25.620
While the Saudi family likes to perpetuate&nbsp;
that their destruction is driven by pure and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:31.020
holy religious reasons, there’s little doubt that&nbsp;
keeping power likely also played a role in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:37.140
decisions. Saudi Arabia is an absolutely monarchy&nbsp;
meaning that they still have kings and princes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:42.360
these are the guys that rule over the country.&nbsp;
They don’t have an elected prime minister or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:48.300
president or anything along those lines. In fact,&nbsp;
they virtually never have elections. Power over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:53.100
the country is slowly passed down within the&nbsp;
royal family alone. History has taught us that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:59.400
such monarchies are almost always overthrown&nbsp;
by rebellions and wars. But, Saudi Arabia has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:04.260
actually had a pretty successful history with&nbsp;
a monarchy. Now, this isn’t to say that Saudi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.180
Arabia has been perfect. They’ve had a rather&nbsp;
shady history when it comes to human rights and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.700
women’s rights. But, neither of these have been&nbsp;
enough to spark rebellions within the country. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:21.180
the key reason for this is that the kingdom has&nbsp;
given it’s people the 3 gs: god, gold, and glory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:25.140
In terms of god, it’s clear that they’re&nbsp;
supporting the prevailing form of Islam within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:30.600
the kingdom, Wahhabism, to the maximum extent.&nbsp;
Most Muslims within the kingdom are either netural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:37.500
regarding this issue or they actually support&nbsp;
the destruction. “This is good. الحمدلله We don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:43.080
worship/decorate graves. This proves it.” Most of&nbsp;
the Muslims that are unhappy with the destruction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:48.540
are located outside the kingdom, so they don’t&nbsp;
present that much of a threat to the Saudi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:53.880
family’s power. In terms of gold, Saudi Arabia&nbsp;
has literally stacked their reserves with nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:59.400
half a trillion dollars worth of cash of gold. And&nbsp;
they have extremely lenient taxation and welfare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:05.460
policies when it comes to Saudi nationals. In&nbsp;
fact, Saudi Arabia has no personal income tax. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.780
most Saudi nationals have no complaints&nbsp;
when it comes to the economy. And finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:15.600
in terms of glory, Saudi Arabia is literally the&nbsp;
most prominent Islamic country in the world both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:22.200
religiously and economically. When Saudi citizens&nbsp;
are getting all three gs, they have very little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:28.020
reason to rebel or question the power of the Saudi&nbsp;
family. But, imagine for a second if Saudi Arabia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:33.480
didn’t destroy these historical buildings. Not&nbsp;
only would they not be appeasing the Wahabis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:38.580
within the country, but they would simultaneously&nbsp;
be creating an opportunity for non Wahhabi beliefs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:44.220
to grow and prosper within the kingdom. This is&nbsp;
clearly not something that they want given that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:49.500
they try to discredit historical sites with every&nbsp;
opportunity that they get. For example, Muhammed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:54.180
the Prophet’s apparent birth place is surrounded&nbsp;
by signs in four languages that tell visitors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:59.880
that there is no proof that Muhammed was actually&nbsp;
born there. If the Saudi’s didn’t do this, they’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:04.800
just be asking for non-Wahhabi sects to grow which&nbsp;
would not only create tension between this group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:10.380
and the government but also between this group and&nbsp;
the rest of Saudi Arabia. So, you’d essentially be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:15.960
cultivating a rebellion or a civil war. You’ll see&nbsp;
people questioning the power of the Saudi family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:21.600
and you’ll probably see some religious figure rise&nbsp;
up and lead the revolution. And based on history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:27.060
religion based conflict is usually the most&nbsp;
danegerous form of conflict given that both sides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:32.880
have unbreakable beliefs. I don’t know about you,&nbsp;
but I don’t think the Saudi Royal family wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:38.280
end up like the Iranian Shah. So, they likely&nbsp;
wont be stopping the destruction anytime soon.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:42.420
ESCALATING RESENTMENT:&nbsp;

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:47.040
While the Saudi’s policy of destruction has played&nbsp;
out decently well within Saudi Arabia itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:53.460
the same cannot be said about non-Wahhabi muslims.&nbsp;
To many of them, Saudi Arabia’s actions lack even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:58.320
the basics of decency. In the modern world,&nbsp;
just because you don’t agree with another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:03.840
person’s religion does not mean that you get to&nbsp;
go destroy their history. And even if these sites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:08.400
aren’t holy like the Saudi’s claim, they’re at&nbsp;
the very least important to their own history and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:13.260
culture. The Saudi’s decision to destroy these&nbsp;
sites despite this connection has come off as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.480
extremism to many. The common belief amongst&nbsp;
these people is that the Saudi family’s ego&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:24.840
is way too high and that they’re putting control&nbsp;
and profits over history and culture. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:29.640
it’s not like they had to destroy these sites&nbsp;
to even build their hotels in the first place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:35.340
There’s plenty of space on the outskirts of Mecca&nbsp;
where insane hotels and resorts could have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:41.280
built instead. It’s not just non-Wahhabi muslims&nbsp;
that are upset with Saudi Arabia’s actions either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:47.220
Historians and archeologisits are also not a&nbsp;
fan of this behavior either. These historical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:51.480
buildings likely would’ve given more context&nbsp;
as to how people survived on the peninsula&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:57.900
for past several millenia. For them, this is not&nbsp;
just a matter of protecting Islamic history but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:03.180
a matter of human history. Many historians&nbsp;
and activists have been posting pictures of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:08.100
Islamic historial sites on social media to try to&nbsp;
raise awareness surrounding the situation. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:13.740
this hasn’t really done all that much because&nbsp;
no one is willing to speak out against Saudi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:18.240
Arabia. Neighboring Muslim countries don’t want&nbsp;
Saudi Arabia to reduce their hajj pilgrimage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:24.600
quotas. Meanwhile, western countries don’t want to&nbsp;
jeopardize their source of oil. The only exception&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:29.760
to this is the former president of religious&nbsp;
affairs of Turkey, Mehmet Gormez. He told the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:35.100
Saudi minister of the Hajj that the skyscraper&nbsp;
overshadowing the Kaaba destroys history. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:41.160
honestly, I don’t think the Saudis really cared&nbsp;
about his thoughts. So, while resentment is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:46.680
building outside the kingdom, this probably wont&nbsp;
be leading to any sort of change anytime soon.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:50.820
THE STATE OF MECCA:&nbsp;

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:56.280
In the end, the destruction of much of Mecca&nbsp;
is truly quite a shame. Whether these places&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:01.380
are holy or not, their important pieces of human&nbsp;
history that should be studied and appreciated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:06.660
But instead, the Saudis have been slowly&nbsp;
destroying the city for hundreds of years and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:11.460
this has especially accelerated within the past&nbsp;
few decades. They justify their destruction by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:16.680
claiming that these sites lead to sins and that&nbsp;
they’re not in line with the Wahhabi way. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:22.320
while they don’t admit it, it seems like keeping&nbsp;
control and power also plays a major role this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.780
decision. While this has angered many Muslims and&nbsp;
non-Muslims alike, there’s simply not much that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:32.820
anyone can do about it. After all, it’s not&nbsp;
like the Saudi’s are going over to Egypt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:37.560
destroying their pyramids. The Saudi’s are&nbsp;
simply destroying their own buildings. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:42.420
you can’t do much more than just give&nbsp;
them another perspective. Whether they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:48.000
continue the destruction or not is completely&nbsp;
up to them. Did you realize that Saudi Arabia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:53.340
was destroying their own history? Comment that&nbsp;
down below. Also, drop a like if you hope these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:57.960
sites rest in peace. And of course, consider&nbsp;
checking out our discord community to suggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.800
future video ideas and consider subscribing&nbsp;
